1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,716
Minus twenty degrees of freezing cold...

2
00:00:02,716 --> 00:00:06,091
A snowstorm all around, a bone-biting wind.

3
00:00:06,091 --> 00:00:11,737
In weather like that, do you know what happens if a normal person steps out without clothes?

4
00:00:11,737 --> 00:00:15,531
In just five to ten minutes, the blood vessels constrict.

5
00:00:15,531 --> 00:00:20,941
After twenty minutes, body temperature drops dangerously and hypothermia sets in.

6
00:00:20,941 --> 00:00:26,888
Within half an hour, the heart stops and the body freezes like an ice doll and dies!

7
00:00:26,888 --> 00:00:30,097
This is an absolute rule written by medical science!

8
00:00:30,097 --> 00:00:34,134
But... on that same minus-twenty-degree Himalayan snow...

9
00:00:34,134 --> 00:00:40,618
what if monks sit for hours with nothing on but a thin cotton cloth?

10
00:00:40,618 --> 00:00:44,374
And if cloths soaked in ice water are draped over their bodies...

11
00:00:44,374 --> 00:00:50,370
what if, instead of freezing, those wet cloths steam and dry from their body heat?

12
00:00:50,370 --> 00:00:53,971
Hello everyone, welcome to Be Practical With Kishore!

13
00:00:53,971 --> 00:00:55,424
This is not just a story...

14
00:00:55,424 --> 00:01:04,170
It's an absolute reality that world-famous Harvard University medical scientists tested themselves in the hills of Ladakh and showed the world!

15
00:01:04,170 --> 00:01:07,417
Meanwhile in Europe, a man named Wim Hof...

16
00:01:07,417 --> 00:01:11,197
runs through Arctic Circle snow wearing only shorts,

17
00:01:11,197 --> 00:01:15,820
sits neck-deep in a box of pure ice cubes for two hours,

18
00:01:15,820 --> 00:01:22,067
and even with dangerous bacteria injected into his blood, he neutralises it with his internal heat!

19
00:01:22,067 --> 00:01:27,006
How can a fire blaze inside the human body in freezing snow?

20
00:01:27,006 --> 00:01:30,974
How can human willpower control body temperature?

21
00:01:30,974 --> 00:01:34,929
Let us practically break down the science of fire and ice!

22
00:01:36,529 --> 00:01:43,231
The ancient secret behind this mystery is called... Tummo, or inner fire meditation.

23
00:01:43,231 --> 00:01:49,570
Handed down for thousands of years in the Tibetan Buddhist tradition, this practice is also called Chandali yoga.

24
00:01:49,570 --> 00:01:56,359
Lamas who practise it live in mountain caves in sub-zero cold, wearing only thin cloth.

25
00:01:56,359 --> 00:02:01,485
Hearing of this, a leading professor at Harvard Medical School, Dr. Herbert Benson...

26
00:02:01,485 --> 00:02:06,422
went to the Himalayas himself with his research team in 1982.

27
00:02:06,422 --> 00:02:13,259
The scientists had one question... is this a real biological fact, or are they playing some trick?

28
00:02:13,259 --> 00:02:20,506
They fixed highly sensitive digital thermometers to the monks' fingers, toes and chests.

29
00:02:20,506 --> 00:02:24,774
Normally, in severe cold, finger temperature drops.

30
00:02:24,774 --> 00:02:30,777
But as soon as the monks began Tummo meditation... a wonder happened before the doctors' eyes!

31
00:02:30,777 --> 00:02:38,116
The temperature of the monks' fingers rose steadily... by a full eight to seventeen degrees Fahrenheit!

32
00:02:38,116 --> 00:02:44,302
Even in freezing cold, heat like a central heating system was being generated inside their bodies!

33
00:02:44,302 --> 00:02:47,567
Unable to believe it, the scientists ran a more extreme test.

34
00:02:47,567 --> 00:02:51,125
They put wet cloths dipped in ice water on their shoulders.

35
00:02:51,125 --> 00:02:54,123
A normal person would go into shock from that cold.

36
00:02:54,123 --> 00:03:01,351
But within forty-five minutes... steam rose from the monks' bodies and the wet cloths dried completely!

37
00:03:01,351 --> 00:03:04,226
The Harvard doctors wrote in their research papers:

38
00:03:04,226 --> 00:03:11,693
this is undeniable proof that a person can control the human autonomic nervous system with the power of the mind!

39
00:03:12,893 --> 00:03:19,810
The man who proved this in the modern world, like a superhuman... Wim Hof, The Iceman.

40
00:03:19,810 --> 00:03:23,302
Wim Hof, holder of more than twenty-six Guinness World Records...

41
00:03:23,302 --> 00:03:29,441
even after sitting two hours among blocks of ice, his core body temperature doesn't drop by a single degree.

42
00:03:29,441 --> 00:03:33,617
In 2014, professors at Radboud University in the Netherlands

43
00:03:33,617 --> 00:03:39,184
injected Wim Hof's body with an E. coli toxin that causes a severe infection.

44
00:03:39,184 --> 00:03:43,529
Inject it into a normal person and they get a high fever and shivering.

45
00:03:43,529 --> 00:03:48,725
But Wim Hof, through his special breathing technique, raised his adrenaline levels...

46
00:03:48,725 --> 00:03:53,494
completely suppressed the infection and stunned the doctors!

47
00:03:53,494 --> 00:03:55,879
Now the real practical question:

48
00:03:55,879 --> 00:04:00,230
scientifically, how is so much heat generated in our body?

49
00:04:00,230 --> 00:04:06,960
There is a secret behind it. That is... Brown Adipose Tissue, or Brown Fat!

50
00:04:06,960 --> 00:04:09,597
Our body has two kinds of fat.

51
00:04:09,597 --> 00:04:14,927
One is White Fat, which stores calories and makes us fat.

52
00:04:14,927 --> 00:04:19,755
The second is Brown Fat. It is packed with iron-rich mitochondria.

53
00:04:19,755 --> 00:04:24,401
These are like furnaces, tiny fire pits, inside our body!

54
00:04:24,401 --> 00:04:28,379
When we do deep breathing and special breathing methods...

55
00:04:28,379 --> 00:04:32,731
signals go out from the brain and this Brown Fat suddenly ignites.

56
00:04:32,731 --> 00:04:36,569
It turns calories directly into pure heat!

57
00:04:36,569 --> 00:04:40,170
In science this is called non-shivering thermogenesis.

58
00:04:40,170 --> 00:04:45,480
That is, without the body shivering, an internal heater switches on!

59
00:04:45,480 --> 00:04:51,572
Yogis who practise Tummo use this breathing along with vase breathing and mental focus...

60
00:04:51,572 --> 00:04:55,566
and tune the mind as if heat were flowing up the spine.

61
00:04:55,566 --> 00:05:06,748
Tummo and the Wim Hof science are undeniable evidence that the mind can rule the body, that human will can withstand the forces of nature!

62
00:05:06,748 --> 00:05:10,167
What do you think about this mystery of ice and fire?

63
00:05:10,167 --> 00:05:13,303
Be sure to tell us your opinion in the comments below.

64
00:05:13,303 --> 00:05:15,998
If you liked this video, like and share it.

